- Technical Details
    - Tech Stack:
        - Python 3.11 plus
        - Data: yfinance, pandas, pyarrow, DuckDB
        - Backtesting: vectorbt, quantstats, empyrical-reloaded, arch
        - Dashboard: plotly static HTML, GitHub Pages
        - Scheduling: GitHub Actions cron
    - Key Files:
        - src/isa/prices.py: per-ticker Parquet store and DuckDB universe reader
        - src/isa/fetch.py: incremental price fetch and update with injectable fetcher
        - src/isa/universe.py: resolve all, ticker, sector, index, theme specs
        - src/isa/seed_categories.py: seed sectors and membership from Wikipedia S&P 500
        - src/isa/strategy.py: META interface and auto-discovery of strategies
        - src/isa/engine.py: vectorbt backtest engine and core metrics
        - src/isa/stats.py: stationary bootstrap confidence intervals
        - src/isa/results.py: append-only results store and equity curves
        - src/isa/runner.py: orchestrates strategy x universe runs
        - src/isa/build_site.py: static Plotly dashboard generation
        - src/isa/cli.py: isa CLI with seed, update, run, build
        - strategies/: one file per strategy, discovered automatically
    - Architecture Notes:
        - Thin glue over mature FOSS, not a framework
        - Each ticker is an independent Parquet file, queried by DuckDB glob
        - CI bounds stored at write time so the dashboard stays read-only and fast
        - Everything runnable locally via the same CLI the workflow calls

